 {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "node_degree", "args": {"nodes": [28, 243, 617, 1752], "window": [4765, 43165]}, "result_digest": "7fcbf9a0f4e54a41", "result_summary": "{\"nodes\": [{\"distinct_partners\": 299, \"events\": 383, \"node\": 28}, {\"distinct_partners\": 7, \"events\": 7, \"node\": 243}, {\"distinct_partners\": 5, \"events\": 5, \"node\": 617}, {\"distinct_partners\": 10, \"events\": 11, \"node\": 1752}], \"window\": [4765, 43165]}", "latency_ms": 10, "tokens_before": 30158, "tokens_after": 30158, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_44f03991", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1330, 361], "window": [4765, 43165], "confidence": 0.95, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Source 1330 emits and receives nothing inside [4765,43165]; its entire activity (7 events) begins only after t=43166. A cascade needs at least one outgoing event from the source within the window to start a <=600-unit time-respecting chain, so none can exist. The apparent connection is purely static: over all time 1330 links to 678, and hub 28 (383 events, 299 partners) contacts 361, giving a time-ignored path 1330->678->28->361. That path plus the high overall volume (5150 events) and 361's in-window activity are the confounders; they do not create a temporal cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings**\n\n- **Node 1330 has zero events in [4765, 43165]** \u2014 0 events, 0 distinct partners, empty neighbour set and an empty 2-hop subgraph (steps 02, 03, 04).\n- 1330 *is* active in the dataset overall (7 events, step 05), but all of them fall **after** the window: 0 events in [0, 4764], 7 events in [43166, 100000], with its first event landing in [43166, 44000] (steps 06, 14). So its entire activity postdates the interval, and nothing it does can seed a cascade inside it.\n- Target 361 *is* active in the window (4 events, partners {28, 243, 617, 1752}, steps 02, 08, 12), so the absence is one-sided: there is a receiver but no emitter.\n- **Confounder controls:** (a) *Time-ignored connectivity* \u2014 over all time 1330 does sit in a large connected component via 399/669/678/681/724, and 678\u219228, 28\u2192361 exist, so a static path 1330\u2192678\u219228\u2192361 \"exists\" if timestamps are discarded (steps 10, 13). (b) *Popularity/volume* \u2014 28 is a massive hub (383 events, 299 partners in-window) and the window holds 5150 events among 1901 nodes (steps 01, 15), so a static path through 28 is essentially guaranteed by hub-ness, not by influence. (c) 1330's in-window one-hop neighbourhood candidates (669, 678, 681, 724, 1484) are active in the window (step 11), yet none of that activity can be downstream of 1330 because 1330 emits nothing until t \u2248 43166+.\n\nSince a \u2264600-unit time-respecting chain requires at least one outgoing event from 1330 inside the window, and there are none, no such cascade can exist.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1330, 361],\n  \"window\": [4765, 43165],\n  \"confidence\": 0.95,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Source 1330 emits and receives nothing inside [4765,43165]; its entire activity (7 events) begins only after t=43166. A cascade needs at least one outgoing event from the source within the window to start a <=600-unit time-respecting chain, so none can exist. The apparent connection is purely static: over all time 1330 links to 678, and hub 28 (383 events, 299 partners) contacts 361, giving a time-ignored path 1330->678->28->361. That path plus the high overall volume (5150 events) and 361's in-window activity are the confounders; they do not create a temporal cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 37687, "total_output_tokens": 3800, "total_tokens": 41487, "total_latency_ms": 59582, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}